#: docs/specifications/capabilities/README.md
msgid "Capabilities"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/README.md
msgid "Each capability is something the platform must be able to do, and each has a contract made of numbered clauses. The words `MUST`, `SHOULD` and `MAY` are used as in [BCP 14]{1} (RFC 2119 and RFC 8174), and only the upper-case forms are requirements. Every clause also says how conformance is shown, so an implementation can prove that it meets the clause rather than just claim it."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/README.md
msgid "The clause text lives in [`blueprint/catalogue.yaml`]{1}, and the tables on each page are generated from it by `just render`."
msgstr ""

